<title>UK: Halifax CEO to head UK bankers' group - Time.</title>
<headline>Halifax CEO to head UK bankers' group - Time.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mike Blackburn, chief executive of Britain's Halifax Plc will become the next president of the Chartered Institute of Bankers (CIB), The Times newspaper said on Monday.</p>
<p>The Times said Blackburn would succeed Brian Pitman, chairman of Lloyds TSB Group Plc next year. The report said Blackburn's appointment signalled the Halifax's new-found status as a bank.</p>
<p>The former building society converted to bank status this year.</p>
